---

## Error Handling
When implementing features:
- Catch and log all exceptions; never fail silently
- Upwork MCP session expired? → Run `uv run upwork-mcp --login` in `/home/gio/Tools/upwork-mcp`
- Google Docs token expired? → Delete `~/.mekhani/token.json` to trigger re-auth
- Apify quota exceeded? → Check plan at apify.com
- Claude API error? → Check `ANTHROPIC_API_KEY` and account credits
- Telegram flood wait? → Bot auto-retries (check `logs/mekhani.log`)

---

## Testing & QA
- Run tests before any commit: `pytest tests/`
- Test platform connections: `python main.py --test-upwork` (etc.)
- Always use `--dry-run` for end-to-end testing without side effects
- Check logs for errors: `tail -f logs/mekhani.log`

---

## Commits
Use Sentry conventional format:
- `feat: add Upwork scraper with MCP integration`
- `fix: handle Apify rate limiting gracefully`
- `refactor: extract Job model validation to shared library`
- `docs: update setup guide for Google Docs OAuth`

---

## Integration with positronica_core
Always import from the shared library:
```python
from positronica_core.db import Job, init_db, bulk_insert_jobs
from positronica_core.config import settings
from positronica_core.filters import match_cv, score_job
from positronica_core.llm import ClaudeClient
from positronica_core.notifiers import TelegramNotifier, GoogleDocsClient
```

If positronica_core changes break Mekhani, check the core changelog and update imports immediately.
